nuary of 2020.  her remains were found over a month  later an autopsy revealed she died of  blunt force trauma and a gunshot wound  to the head well cell phone records and  surveillance video put gooch at the  scene of the crime previous cell phone  records obtained to show that gooch and  his brothers show contempt towards those  in the mennonite faith mark gooch is  charged with first degree murder and  faces life in prison if found guilty  now for gavel to gavel live coverage of  the trial tune into law in crime network  and when we come back kim potter's  defense team wants this newly upgraded  charge dismissed what lies ahead for the  ex-cop charged with the killing of dante  wright  [Music]  welcome back to law and crime daily we  look now to minnesota where the  attorneys representing kim potter  request a dismissal in her recently  added first degree manslaughter charge  to her case  the former minnesota police officer is  charged with fatally shooting dante  wright during a routine traffic stop in  april of 2021  during that stop potter discharged her  gun allegedly thinking it was her taser  well she shot the 20-year-old before he  sped away and he later died  wright's death along with those of  george floyd and philando castile  sparked outrage across the country after  all three black men were shot and killed  by minnesota police officers the  minnesota attorney general added  potter's first degree manslaughter  charge earlier this month which has a  maximum sentence of 15 years potter's  attorneys filed a motion on wednesday to  dismiss this upgraded charge  back with us is civil rights attorney  jeff storms who represents dante  wright's family so jeff what sort of  reaction are we seeing from the wright  family  well i mean i think that uh repeatedly  the family has felt like they're going  to be efforts by  officer potter to dodge responsibility  for her actions  and you know this would be another clear  example  of that you know the family was very 